# Merged workspace rules (Cursor-era)

Older VS Copilot file: `.github/copilot-instructions.md` (keep in sync). Longer docs stay source for details; this file is what I follow when they conflict. Update this as the workflow changes.

## Communication

- Be concise. Confirm work as best-effort implemented.
- Several questions in one message: one table, one row per question. Columns are Question and Answer. Use their wording in the first column. Do not answer those questions as separate paragraphs. This is not the issue-fix table.
- A recap of more than one item: one table, one row per item. Name the columns for what the recap is listing. Do not recap those items as separate paragraphs. This is not the issue-fix table.
- Table columns do not need to be the same width. Do not set a width to even them out.
- In a table cell, ordered steps are a numbered list. A simple list is bullets.
- Do not say ready to test in-game unless **live game Mods** files were updated in that run.
- Token-heavy work with a cheaper script/CLI/Playwright path: ask first. See `.cursor/rules/token-cost-notice.mdc`.
- Do not markdown-link files/canvases to open them. Touch the file with an editor tool so the chat Open chip appears. See `.cursor/rules/open-files-via-chip.mdc`.

## Lanes

| Lane | Role |
|---|---|
| `01_Draft` | Default for new / `0.x.x` WIP. MakeNewMod creates mods here. |
| `02_ActiveBuild` | Tested pack set. Publish source. **Do not edit or copy into unless asked.** |
| `03_ReleaseSource` | Publish mirror. **Scripts only unless asked.** |
| Game Mods | What the game loads. **Default test deploy.** |
| Dedicated server Mods | Extra DLL test path (below). |
| `00_Tools` | Public/release tools (not game mods). `ModSync`, `LogReader`. Not Draft/ActiveBuild. |
| `00_DLL-Projects` | DLL / generator source (generators that **build mods**). Workshop helpers stay in `Tools/`. |
| `05_ReleaseData/ReadmeSystem` | README templates, `HELPER_ModCompatibility.csv`, quotes. |

New mod: wait for `RUN-MakeNewMod.bat`, then edit **Config** (and helper CSV if needed). Do not invent a mod folder.
Public/release tools: `00_Tools/` (not a game mod; do not use MakeNewMod or Draft/ActiveBuild).

Default test deploy (Cursor-era, from old Copilot):

- Client: `C:/Program Files (x86)/Steam/steamapps/common/7 Days To Die/Mods`
- DLL also: `C:/Program Files (x86)/Steam/steamapps/common/7 Days to Die Dedicated Server/Mods`

Do not promote Draft → ActiveBuild yourself. Official ActiveBuild ↔ game sync is `RUN-Update.bat` / sync-work (user runs). Scripts own rename, README generate, zips.

## What I edit vs scripts

- New Config xpath XML root: `AGF-{last Name segment}`. See `.cursor/rules/mod-xml-root-name.mdc`.
- **I may edit:** Config, loc, DLL/generator source, `00_Tools`, helper CSV, research notes, rules when asked.
- **Not without explicit ask:** ModInfo, README.txt/md, changelog, version bumps, lane promotion. See `.cursor/rules/modinfo-readme-permission.mdc`.
- Mod scope (type 1–5, EAC, safe install/remove): `HELPER_ModCompatibility.csv`, not hand-written README scope.

## Evidence

- Do not guess. Read vanilla `Data/Config` (decompile if DLL), then this repo.
- Unverified if source was not checked. Code/config wins over old README wording.
- Research: `00_Support/WorkspaceData/Research/` plus on-demand rules (blocks flatten, screamer).
- Loc: `.cursor/rules/localization-quality.mdc` (always on). Blocks flatten and screamer/heatmap stay on-demand.

## README wording (when asked)

Follow `05_ReleaseData/ReadmeSystem/WORKFLOW-AI-README-Review.md`. One mod, one section. Suggest (two options + recommended) unless asked to implement. Wait for DONE before version/changelog.

## Purple Book (when that generator)

- Logic only: `00_DLL-Projects/Generators/AGF-PurpleBookGenerator-v0.0.1/Generator/SCRIPT-PurpleBookGenerator.py`
- Default run: `--no-sync-game-mod --no-sync-activebuild`. Live sync only if asked.
- Schematics opener stays `iconbutton`; tint keys `color_default/hovered/selected/disabled`; `color(...)` is RGBA.
- Unlock review: non-magazine; schematic/book only; exclude gas/thrown/dart ammo; keep rocket.

## 7D2D UI look-here

**Before HUD / menu / pause / XUi XML / UI canvas work:** Read `.cursor/rules/7d2d-xui-v3.1.mdc` (scale vs wrap, 16:9 vs 16:10, plates, mock anti-patterns). Do not guess `font_size / 1.255` or fake extra frames.

Vanilla first: `Data/Config/XUi_InGame`, `XUi_Menu`. v3 path is `Config/XUi_InGame` (not old `Config/XUi`). Keep controller-required children or Init NRE. Failed xpath can abort a whole include.

- Menu lifecycle: `00_DLL-Projects/Projects/DLL_NoEAC-AudioOptionsPlus/MCP-7D2D-Menu-Influence-Guide.md`
- Bindings vs patch `<if>`: `00_Support/Automation/workflow/BMCounter-BloodMoon-Source-Workflow.md`
- HUD xpath: `02_ActiveBuild/AGF-HUDPlus-1Main-*/Config/XUi_InGame/`
- Compat: `02_ActiveBuild/zzzAGF-Special-Compatibilities-*/Config/XUi_InGame/ModPatches/`
- Forge dump: `00_Support/WorkspaceData/Research/Forge UI Stuff.md`

Pipeline detail: `00_Support/Automation/workflow/Goals-and-Requirements.md` and `Workflow Outline of Main Script.md`.

7dtdmods first listings: `.cursor/rules/7dtdmods-listing-fill.mdc`.
